{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3268","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3268","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3268\",\"parent_revision\":\"a503063d43c0919d3b278dab2600a755eb51dfc5\",\"root_revision\":\"d1bffde53604e40fbc01e934f4db6be507df276763a9b7446feac66b1f07d43c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nObserved 2026-08-28 while running `/dh:work-backlog-item groom #3169`: dispatching the grooming-swarm agents surfaced two related problems in how the orchestrator is supposed to construct subagent prompts, and a third instance turned up in a different workflow while investigating.\\n\\n**Every other swarm agent's own file requires only `item_ref`/`selector` as input.** Checked directly: `impact-analyst.md`, `fact-checker.md`, `classifier.md`, and `alignment-analyst.md` each declare `## Input` as just `item_ref`/`selector`, and each has an explicit Phase 1 instruction to call `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_view` itself to fetch the item. `backlog-item-groomer.md` is the one exception: its `## Input` section names literal content fields \u2014 item title, item description, research questions, RT-ICA summary \u2014 and the file contains zero `backlog_view` calls anywhere, even though its own frontmatter `tools:` list already includes `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog` (so lack of tool access is not the reason). The orchestrator-facing workflow doc (`skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md`, \\\"Groomer prompt\\\" section) reinforces this by listing an even longer set of content the orchestrator must paste in: title, description, source, priority, plan address, RT-ICA assessment, Fact-Check verdicts, Issue Classification, Root-Cause Analysis, Impact Radius, Research section. Every one of these already exists as a section on the backlog item, reachable by the same `backlog_view` call the other four agents already make themselves \u2014 the groomer's contract just doesn't ask it to. The same document's sequence diagram also nudges toward pasting content for the other four agents (\\\"spawn (item details, ...)\\\", \\\"spawn (item description)\\\") even though those agents' own files are unambiguous about self-fetching \u2014 looser wording, but a contributing cause of the same over-pasting.\\n\\n**Nothing in the swarm.md contract or the agent files constrains what else an orchestrator may write into a dispatch prompt beyond the required input.** During this same grooming run, the orchestrator (this agent) wrote a classifier dispatch prompt that stated its own conclusion \u2014 \\\"this is very likely `defect` ... confirm this classification yourself\\\" \u2014 before the classifier had done any independent reasoning. Nothing in `classifier.md` or `swarm.md` flags this as out of bounds; the only reason it didn't corrupt the result is that the classifier's own 5-whys procedure happened to produce independently-computed evidence (e.g. an exact `difflib.SequenceMatcher` ratio) rather than simply agreeing with the framing it was handed. For a differently-designed agent, or a less careful run, an orchestrator's speculative framing could reach an agent whose entire value is independent verification (fact-checker, classifier, alignment-analyst) and bias its output without any contract violation being detectable after the fact \u2014 the written section would look like an independent verdict either way.\\n\\n**The same pasted-content pattern recurs outside the groom workflow, with a generic executor instead of a specialized one.** `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/close/start.md` Step 5.6 (~line 121) extracts `Acceptance Criteria` from `backlog_view` for the orchestrator's own parsing, then re-types item title, plan address, and each criterion individually into a `dh:task-worker` verification-agent's prompt. `task-worker` already has full `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog` access \u2014 nothing prevents telling it the `item_ref` and the section name and letting it call `backlog_view(selector=item_ref, section=\\\"Acceptance Criteria\\\")` itself, the same way the four self-fetching groom-swarm agents do.\\n\\nAll three instances share a root cause: there is no documented rule for what belongs in a dynamic subagent prompt versus what belongs in the agent's own file or a shared skill (e.g. `dh:subagent-contract`, which four of the five groom-swarm agents already load) versus what the orchestrator must never add (speculative conclusions, pre-formed verdicts). The groomer's contract inconsistency and the close-workflow verification-agent prompt are the concrete, checkable symptoms; the anchoring risk is the less visible consequence of the same missing rule.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T13:44:50.746147Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim 1**: `impact-analyst.md`, `fact-checker.md`, `classifier.md`, and `alignment-analyst.md` each declare `## Input` as just `item_ref`/`selector`\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**Evidence**:\\n- Source: plugins/development-harness/agents/classifier.md:19\\n  Retrieved: 2026-08-28\\n  Content: `- item_ref \u2014 the backlog item reference (#N, title substring, or URL)`\\n- Source: plugins/development-harness/agents/alignment-analyst.md:21\\n  Retrieved: 2026-08-28\\n  Content: `You receive a selector parameter from the orchestrator \u2014 either an issue number (#N), a bare number, or a title substring.`\\n- Source: plugins/development-harness/agents/impact-analyst.md:24\\n  Retrieved: 2026-08-28\\n  Content: `You receive a selector parameter from the orchestrator invocation \u2014 either an issue number (#N), a bare number, or a title substring.`\\n\\n**Claim 2**: These four agents each have an explicit Phase 1 instruction to call `backlog_view` to fetch the item\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED (for three agents; fact-checker differs in dispatch pattern)\\n**Evidence**:\\n- Source: plugins/development-harness/agents/classifier.md:25\\n  Content: `Call mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_view(selector=item_ref, summary=False) and read the item description...`\\n- Source: plugins/development-harness/agents/alignment-analyst.md:100\\n  Content: `Call mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_view(selector=selector, summary=False) to fetch the full item.`\\n- Source: plugins/development-harness/agents/impact-analyst.md:26\\n  Content: `Call mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_view(selector=selector, summary=False) to fetch the full item.`\\n- Note: fact-checker.md is dispatched with claim text, not item_ref; it receives claims to verify, not items to fetch. This is a distinct dispatch pattern from the other three.\\n\\n**Claim 3**: `backlog-item-groomer.md` is the exception with literal content fields in its `## Input` section (title, description, research questions, RT-ICA summary)\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**Evidence**:\\n- Source: plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md:48-53\\n  Content: `## Input` lists: `Item title`, `Item description`, `Research questions`, `RT-ICA summary (optional)`\\n\\n**Claim 4**: `backlog-item-groomer.md` has `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog` in its tools list but contains zero `backlog_view` calls\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**Evidence**:\\n- Source: plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md:4\\n  Content: `tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Skill, SendMessage, mcp__plugin_dh_sam, mcp__plugin_dh_backlog`\\n- Source: grep of backlog-item-groomer.md shows 0 occurrences of \\\"backlog_view\\\"\\n\\n**Claim 5**: `swarm.md`'s \\\"Groomer prompt\\\" section explicitly lists a long set of content the orchestrator must paste (title, description, source, priority, plan address, RT-ICA, Fact-Check, Issue Classification, Root-Cause Analysis, Impact Radius, Research)\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**Evidence**:\\n- Source: plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md\\n  Retrieved: 2026-08-28\\n  Content: `Input to groomer: item title, description, source, priority, plan address, RT-ICA assessment, Fact-Check verdicts, Issue Classification, Root-Cause Analysis (or \\\"N/A\\\"), Impact Radius, Research section`\\n\\n**Claim 6**: Sequence diagram uses looser phrasing like \\\"item details\\\"/\\\"item description\\\" for the other four agents\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**Evidence**:\\n- Source: plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md lines 65-68\\n  Content: Diagram shows `O->>IA: spawn (item details, Files, Evidence, suggested_location)`, `O->>FC: spawn (item claims to verify...)`, `O->>CL: spawn (item description)` \u2014 looser than the actual agent Input sections which state agents must self-fetch with item_ref\\n\\n**Claim 7**: `close/start.md` Step 5.6 (~line 121) re-types item title, plan address, and each criterion individually into a `task-worker` prompt\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**Evidence**:\\n- Source: plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/close/start.md:121\\n  Retrieved: 2026-08-28\\n  Content: `Spawn a verification agent with subagent_type=\\\"dh:task-worker\\\". Prompt must include: item title, plan address (e.g., P{id}), checklist status (100%), and each criterion listed individually as \\\"Criterion N: {text}\\\".`\\n\\n**Claim 8**: `task-worker` already has full `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog` access\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**Evidence**:\\n- Source: plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md\\n  Retrieved: 2026-08-28\\n  Content: `When a role is not declared in the manifest, the harness dispatches dh:task-worker for that role with no specialist profile loaded. task-worker executes the task directly using full dh tool permissions (SAM MCP, backlog MCP).`\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T13:21:50.083980Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-08-28T13:53:18.062041Z \u2014 RT-ICA Final Pass \u2014 replacing initial snapshot after grooming swarm (impact-analyst, fact-checker, classifier, alignment-analyst) completed</summary>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: Grooming-swarm subagent dispatch contract is inconsistent: one agent requires orchestrator-pasted content while the rest self-fetch, and nothing constrains what an orchestrator may add to a dispatch prompt\\nDate: 2026-08-28\\nGoal: Establish a documented rule for what belongs in a dynamic subagent dispatch prompt (item_ref/selector plus genuinely dynamic cross-agent findings) versus what belongs in the agent's own file or a shared skill, versus what the orchestrator must never add (speculative conclusions, pre-formed verdicts) \u2014 and bring the three found instances into line with it.\\nConditions:\\n1. `backlog-item-groomer.md`'s `## Input` section names literal content fields (title, description, research questions, RT-ICA summary) and contains zero `backlog_view` calls, despite having `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog` tool access. | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. `impact-analyst.md`, `fact-checker.md`, `classifier.md`, `alignment-analyst.md` each declare `## Input` as only `item_ref`/`selector` and each has an explicit Phase 1 `backlog_view` self-fetch call. | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. `swarm.md`'s \\\"Groomer prompt\\\" section explicitly lists a long set of content the orchestrator must paste for the groomer (title, description, source, priority, plan address, RT-ICA, Fact-Check, Issue Classification, Root-Cause Analysis, Impact Radius, Research) \u2014 all of which already exist as sections on the item. Its sequence diagram also uses looser \\\"item details\\\"/\\\"item description\\\" phrasing for the other four agents, contributing to over-pasting even though those agents' own files are unambiguous. | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. The classifier-anchoring incident (orchestrator stated its own conclusion before the classifier reasoned) \u2014 happened this session, exact prompt text known, and nothing in `classifier.md` or `swarm.md` prohibits it. | Status: AVAILABLE\\n