ator must never add (speculative conclusions, pre-formed verdicts) \u2014 and bring the three found instances into line with it.\\nConditions:\\n1. backlog-item-groomer.md's ## Input section names literal content fields and contains zero backlog_view calls, despite mcp__plugin_dh_backlog tool access. | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-Check Claim 3/4 \u2014 backlog-item-groomer.md:48-53, tools list:4, zero backlog_view occurrences confirmed by grep.\\n2. impact-analyst.md, fact-checker.md, classifier.md, alignment-analyst.md each declare ## Input as only item_ref/selector and self-fetch via backlog_view. | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-Check Claim 1/2 \u2014 line citations for all four agent files; fact-checker.md dispatched with claim text rather than item_ref (distinct pattern, noted, does not change verdict).\\n3. swarm.md's \\\"Groomer prompt\\\" section lists the full paste-in field set; sequence diagram uses looser phrasing for the other four agents. | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-Check Claim 5/6 \u2014 swarm.md Groomer prompt section and lines 65-68 quoted verbatim.\\n4. Classifier-anchoring incident (orchestrator stated its own conclusion before classifier reasoned) \u2014 happened this session, nothing in classifier.md or swarm.md prohibits it. | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: session-observed at creation time; no contrary evidence found by fact-checker.\\n5. close/start.md Step 5.6 (~line 121) re-types item title, plan address, and each acceptance criterion into a dh:task-worker prompt instead of self-fetch. | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-Check Claim 7/8 \u2014 close/start.md:121 quoted; task-worker's mcp__plugin_dh_backlog access confirmed via backlog-item-lifecycle.md.\\n6. Content of dh:subagent-contract, the shared skill four of the five groom-swarm agents load \u2014 not yet read at snapshot time. | Snapsh